Sales Forecast
==============

Sales forecasts for salable goods only, excluding services, based on confirmed,
processing and completed sales. Quantities are converted to the product's default
unit; sale lines with incompatible unit categories are omitted and reported to
the user.

Calculate forecasts from the main calculation screen. Choose the company,
calendar, date range and optional products, then calculate the desired method.
Calculated results are read-only. Week labels use ISO WW/YY. Historical weekly
comparisons use the same ISO week in the previous year, falling back to week 52
when the previous year has no week 53.

Percentages are entered as percentages in the client (20 means 20%). Existing
stored ratios remain unchanged. A product-specific increase takes precedence
over category increases. Contradictory category increases are rejected. Set the
product family root to limit the suggested categories to your family hierarchy.

Existing historical parameters are reused by default. Select "Refresh Forecast
Parameters" to refresh sales history, distributions and calendar event results.
Missing parameters are initialized automatically, and calendar edits invalidate
the affected cached parameters. Product days are excluded from the weekday
distribution only for the products involved. Special-sale exclusions follow
their product or customer scope.

Weekday distributions cover the last twelve calendar months, including today
and excluding the equivalent date a year ago. Customer-category special sales
exclude products actually sold on the event date, including newly sold products.
Special-sale reference weeks use the same ISO-week rule as General forecasts;
incompatible units are omitted and reported in these calculations too.

Key-account orders and customer truck/pallet quantities retain their weekly
total when distributed over holidays; those explicit quantities take precedence
over calendar event forecasts. Mixed forecasts without orders use General
parameters, including family increases, and calendar events. New Product uses
only months closed both at calculation time and before the forecast period. A
missing closed month with sales raises an error instead of producing a zero.

Manual forecasts preserve their weekly quantity when distributing it over
weekdays and holidays. Partial weeks include only the selected days. Daily
rounding is reconciled with the weekly total. A product day requires an explicit
quantity; zero is allowed. Missing packaging conversion factors are never
replaced by a one-to-one conversion: unavailable boxes/pallets remain empty,
and entering boxes or pallets without the required factors raises an error.

"Forecast vs Actual Sales" compares the latest complete forecast for each
product/week with actual sales, by week or for the entire selected period. It
supports products, family categories, forecast method and units/boxes/pallets.
A missing forecast is shown as N/A, also in aggregates containing a missing
week. An unknown packaging conversion is also N/A. Percentage differences are
N/A when actual sales are zero. Subtotals and a grand total are included.
The product's planning tab also selects the latest complete forecast per week;
recalculating one week keeps the latest results for the other weeks visible.

The customer integration initializes the family root from Familia/Família and
builds calendar product days from sales of products in Diadas/Diades. Dates with
manual edits are preserved when regenerating automatic calendar entries.
